    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0373" n="313" xml:id="pg313"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Eustis to Mr.
                            Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Reply to your two telegrams, Clunet’s opinion is that a Frenchman can sue the
                    State, but not before ordinary judicial tribunals. Such suits can only be
                    brought before what are known here as “administrative” tribunals. No difference
                    in this respect between an alien and a Frenchman.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eustis</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
